  "uv_convention": "Equirectangular. u = (longitude + 180) / 360 with east (positive longitude) to the right; v = (latitude + 90) / 180; PNG top row = north pole (v = 1). Identical to Game.Levels.PlanetCoordinates.ToUv; the globe mesh in PlanetGlobe already uses it.",
  "files": {
    "Albedo": "sRGB colour, unlit, no clouds. Import sRGB, wrap U Repeat / V Clamp, aniso 8.",
    "Height": "16-bit grey, linear. 0.5 = sea level, 0.5..1 land (1 = highest peak), 0..0.5 sea floor.",
    "Normal": "Tangent space from land relief (sea surface flat). R = +east, G = +north (OpenGL / Unity convention, same as GlobePainter.Normals). Import as Normal map.",
    "Mask": "Linear. R land 0/1 (antialiased coast), G specular/wetness (sea 1, lakes 0.85, black ice 0.6, snow ~0.5, dry land ~0.1), B glow strength, A region id (same values as Regions.R).",
    "Regions": "Linear, sample with POINT filtering. R region id on land only, G region id including its sea territory, B soft membership 0..1 for a gentle highlight falloff. id = round(value*255/40).",
    "Emission": "sRGB glow, multiply by an HDR colour/intensity; strongest on the night side.",
    "Clouds": "Linear; cover in R, G, B and A (the existing shaders read .a). Wraps in longitude."
  },
